   "source": [
    "# Crop Disease Detection - Dataset Exploration\n",

    "\n",
    "**Group problem area:** We imagine an application that lets a farmer take a photo of a crop leaf and immediately see an instant disease diagnosis thanks to an ML image classification engine.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Dataset explored:** We have looked at the PlantVillage Dataset, from Hughes and Salathé 2015 which is kept at github.com/spMohanty/PlantVillage-Dataset."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "606def02",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Candidate open source datasets\n",
    "\n",
    "The table below lists the open source datasets considered for this problem area, along with the variable in each that would serve as the **expected output (target label)** of the final application.\n",
    "\n",
    "| # | Dataset | Description | Expected output variable |\n",
    "|---|---------|-------------|---------------------------|\n",
    "| 1 | **PlantVillage** (spMohanty/PlantVillage-Dataset) 54,305 leaf images taken in lab conditions 14 crop species, 38 crop-disease classes disease_label. The crop-disease (or class of the leaf) |\n",
    "| 2 | **New Plant Diseases Dataset** (Kaggle augmented version of PlantVillage, around 87,000 images) Offline-augmented version of PlantVillage same 38 classes disease_label. Crop-disease class |\n",
    "| 3 | **PlantDoc** (Singh et al. 2020) around 2,598 real-world field images (not taken in lab backgrounds) 13 species, 27 classes disease_label. Crop-disease class, under real field conditions |\n",
    "| 4 | **Cassava Leaf Disease Classification** (Kaggle / Makerere AI Lab, around 21,397 images) Field images of cassava leaves collected in Uganda 5 classes (4 diseases plus healthy) disease_class. Cassava disease category |\n",
    "\n",
    "### Why PlantVillage was selected\n",
    "- It is the largest and most balanced in terms of classes among the candidates with 54,305 labeled images spread across 38 classes.\n",
    "- It is the commonly used dataset, in plant disease classification research, which helps in checking how well our model works compared to results that have already been published.\n",
    "- The dataset was originally curated specifically to support the development of **mobile** disease diagnostic tools using machine learning  a direct match for our project's ML + Mobile App approach."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a8f5cef9",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "1234d6b5",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Fetching the dataset\n",
    "\n",
    "The dataset is organized as one folder per crop-disease class under `raw/color`."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "dd781ff7",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Clone only the raw/color portion of the PlantVillage repository\n",
    "!git clone --filter=blob:none --no-checkout --depth 1 https://github.com/spMohanty/PlantVillage-Dataset.git\n",
    "%cd PlantVillage-Dataset\n",
    "!git sparse-checkout init --cone\n",
    "!git sparse-checkout set raw/color\n",
    "!git checkout master\n",
    "%cd .."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "bb99f9f6",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Building the working dataframe\n",
    "\n",
    "Since this is an image dataset "rows". Columns" refer to a metadata table we construct. Each row represents one image and the columns provide details about that image. These details include the file path, the crop species, the disease label, the health status, the file format and the size. We organize the information this way so each image has its row with all relevant data, in the correct columns. This metadata table is what the exploration questions below are answered against."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "28eed493",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import os\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "\n",
    "DATA_DIR = \"PlantVillage-Dataset/raw/color\"\n",
    "\n",
    "records = []\n",
    "for class_folder in os.listdir(DATA_DIR):\n",
    "    class_path = os.path.join(DATA_DIR, class_folder)\n",
    "    if not os.path.isdir(class_path):\n",
    "        continue\n",
    "    if \"___\" in class_folder:\n",
    "        crop, disease = class_folder.split(\"___\", 1)\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        crop, disease = class_folder, \"unknown\"\n",
    "    for filename in os.listdir(class_path):\n",
    "        filepath = os.path.join(class_path, filename)\n",
    "        records.append({\n",
    "            \"filepath\": filepath,\n",
    "            \"crop_species\": crop,\n",
    "            \"disease_label\": disease,\n",
    "            \"is_healthy\": disease.lower() == \"healthy\",\n",
    "            \"file_extension\": filename.split(\".\")[-1].lower(),\n",
    "            \"file_size_kb\": round(os.path.getsize(filepath) / 1024, 2)\n",
    "        })\n",
    "\n",
    "df = pd.DataFrame(records)\n",
    "df.head()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "9aa0614d",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
